e following Peter commemoration, is read in all three witnesses. Both older witnesses actually print natalitia;1962 prints natalicia. The exact accepted same-word pair is neuter accusative plural, the direct object of colimus in both full contexts. No commemorationem is substituted. Printed1962 cuius/eius are represented by established calendar cujus/ejus. Pustet omits the target comma after ut; Mame prints a colon after quaesumus where target has a semicolon. Pustet actually ends Per Dominum.; Mame actually ends only Per.; the1962 Paul paragraph has no conclusion or cue and ends sentiamus. It is followed by Et fit commemoratio S.Petri Ap.sub unica conclusione and a distinct Peter Oratio2924. Neither historical cue nor Peter ending is supplied to Paul.","locator":"Own June30 Pustet1862 PDF[562],printed476;Mame1922 PDF[754],printed640","source_ids":["artifact.triptych.roman-1962-latin-proper-editorial-projection.editorial-projection-2026-10-23-paul-june30.three-primary-petitions-20261023","artifact.catholic-church.missale-romanum.pustet-ratisbon-1862.paul-june30-primary-petitions-20261023","artifact.catholic-church.missale-romanum.pustet-ratisbon-1862.ia-facsimile-pdf-363d6fc3","artifact.catholic-church.missale-romanum.1922-tours-mame-editio-quarta-iuxta-typicam.ia-scan-pdf-9873693a","artifact.charlton-t-lewis.a-latin-dictionary.harper-new-york-1879.lexical-spellings-facsimile-e5c044e6","artifact.joseph-henry-allen.new-latin-grammar.ginn-1903.identity-and-grammar-facsimile-c992ef6b"],"status":"permitted","surfaces":["cli","corpus-data","download","print","public-git","web"]},"reason":null,"text_sha256":"b2f29e451a2ba64f2a1fb01732ac5c4503f3ba81e70f9c8c483637088e0218b1","withheld":false},"name":"Collect","source":"composed","taken_from":null,"text":"Deus, qui multitudinem gentium beati Pauli Apostoli praedicatione docuisti:\nda nobis, quaesumus; ut, cujus natalicia colimus, ejus apud te patrocinia\nsentiamus.\n","text_status":null,"translations":null,"unavailable_trans